From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:32:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 439/488] [DS4.1] Run 18 fixes: InputBatch methods, bitmask
 stand-in, Engram test backend

- input_batch.py: the logits_rows helpers sat between InputBatch's
  fields and make_dummy, which they swallowed (make_dummy became dead
  code inside a function). They follow the class now.
- The grammar bitmask's unread input-index stand-in was cu_num_logits
  converted to int64 on every call, one more launch (run 18: +1.2 us at
  one request); an empty int64 tensor stands in.
- test_engram_gates_only_the_real_local_rows stubs the B12X mix; it pins
  the B12X path whatever backend the process selects.
---
 tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py |  2 ++
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/input_batch.py             | 32 +++++++++----------
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/tilelang_structured.py     |  8 +++--
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py
